Sval: accessibility checks a shadow host's unslotted children once per walk

`DocAccessible::PruneOrInsertSubtree` checked the containing shadow host's
explicit children, and called `ContentRemoved` on each one without a frame,
for every node it walked inside that host's shadow tree. Framing a subtree
of a shadow tree again cost (nodes walked) x (host's children). Chrome's
popups and panels are shadow hosts whose children have no frame while
closed, and a long-lived window keeps every one it has built, so with an
accessibility client on each update of the chrome took seconds late in a
session. The walk reaches every node of the shadow tree, so checking at the
host itself or at the insert root covers each host once.

diff --git a/accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp b/accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp
index 7e0c5dc85a..00670fc15b 100644
--- a/accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp
+++ b/accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp
@@ -1461,12 +1461,17 @@ bool DocAccessible::PruneOrInsertSubtree(nsIContent* aRoot,
       aRoot->GetShadowRoot() ? aRoot : aRoot->GetContainingShadowHost();
   if (shadowHost) {
     // Check all explicit children in the host, if they are not slotted
-    // then remove their accessibles and subtrees.
-    for (nsIContent* childNode = shadowHost->GetFirstChild(); childNode;
-         childNode = childNode->GetNextSibling()) {
-      if (!childNode->GetPrimaryFrame() &&
-          !nsCoreUtils::CanCreateAccessibleWithoutFrame(childNode)) {
-        ContentRemoved(childNode);
+    // then remove their accessibles and subtrees. The walk below reaches
+    // every node of the host's shadow tree, so the host's children are
+    // checked at the host or at the insert root, once per walk, rather than
+    // again for each node inside its shadow tree.
+    if (aIsInsertRoot || shadowHost == aRoot) {
+      for (nsIContent* childNode = shadowHost->GetFirstChild(); childNode;
+           childNode = childNode->GetNextSibling()) {
+        if (!childNode->GetPrimaryFrame() &&
+            !nsCoreUtils::CanCreateAccessibleWithoutFrame(childNode)) {
+          ContentRemoved(childNode);
+        }
       }
     }
 
